# Code-tree hygiene

Daily layout is a single NeoForge module. Hide local junk; do not rearrange
reference trees or generated datapacks as a cleanup.

## Never

- `git clean -fdx`, delete, junction, or symlink `gt6_code/`,
  `gtceu_code/`, `gt6u_code/`, `gt6_dump/`, `gt6_referencable_port_code/`,
  or `ktfruaddon/`
- Add a new `src/<name>_generated` sibling. Frozen roots live in
  `tools/generated_resource_roots.json` and
  `gradle/scripts/source-sets.gradle`
- Drop a new tracked file at `tools/` root. Put wave ledgers under
  `tools/waves/<slug>/`, builders next to their package, scratch in
  `tools/scratch/` or `tools/_tmp_*.py` (gitignored)
- Delete Java, Python, or GameTest tests to look more like GT6
- Move hashed `tools/*.json` or GameTest classes without a dedicated card
- `git add` closed-card `tools/**/*.log` or closed-wave / tools-root dump
  evidence (`source.json`, `*_source.json`, `dump_slice.json`, player-path,
  census-delta, `census.json`, `*.currentness.json`, and the other evidence
  names in `.gitignore`). Those stay on disk for local replay. Do not untrack
  the current unique-active wave under
  `tools/waves/worldgen/gt-stone-layer-rocks/`, or `--check` manifests such as
  `gt6_pipe_source.json`

## Do

- Local Minecraft instances belong in `run/` or `run-*/` (gitignored)
- Scratch extractors stay gitignored until a card promotes them
- New Python tests must be listed in `python_test_policy.json` as `active`,
  `manual_replay`, or `historical`
- New GameTests go in `src/test/java/.../gametest` (or the existing test
  package for scale/census holders). Do not put GameTest classes back in
  `src/main` or split one holder package across source sets
